{"title":"Mock AIME 1 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is a rectangular sheet of paper. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are points on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> respectively such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/b/e8b38b422f45fb627782b5b44993697c84e16e85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE &lt; CF$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"81\" height=\"13\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/8/9182fd187d738b152f8fb896d002b01dbb55571d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCFE$\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" /> is folded over <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c128243ea8125d0bb007b8132dcfa44461df73a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> maps to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/7/9b798193cb94562989018728e1151587c618655b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"16\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> maps to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/7/4c71f19552a05ee5e2b31e94aff3fb986884bf31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;$\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/4/4c4aab985e86bd50e3ef1508e34cd46727693e2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{AB&#39;C&#39;} \\cong \\angle{B&#39;EA}$\" width=\"149\" height=\"14\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/9/8794aa08f19b32695b27abb5da3e0b22ec3ccd97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB&#39; = 5$\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/6/fd6757f321d37517485d1c3c16189e9f91ab9a19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE = 23$\" width=\"71\" height=\"12\" />, then the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/9/779b978ea913269de34f03258ecb67fb81ab239b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b\\sqrt{c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" /> square units, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/7/9f73d811eca6419d9c9a27423331d71ff06eb957.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"29\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are integers and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is not divisible by the square of any prime. Compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/d/2cdfeae33c1e09de6207d446beb72396c04be481.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b + c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/2/8424728004e41245f232f824d5164e1f7bbedb0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{AB&#39;C&#39;} = \\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"100\" height=\"16\" />. By some angle chasing in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/2/c42ea0f591607fba13802970cd4202180f92ad24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{AB&#39;E}$\" width=\"63\" height=\"14\" />, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/1/e21f23ed49ca394e51d72bae1936909e4d956939.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{EAB&#39;} = 90^{\\circ} - 2 \\theta$\" width=\"150\" height=\"14\" />. Before we apply the law of sines, we're going to want to get everything in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/5/865211471c7cc8aff3d88f9f2b843bd262159050.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin \\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"36\" height=\"14\" />, so note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/6/4562609261d515efd15a41a8faf9f277fff1ce94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin \\angle{EAB&#39;} = \\sin(90^{\\circ} - 2 \\theta) = \\cos 2 \\theta = 1 - 2 \\sin^2 \\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"391\" height=\"20\" />. Now, we use law of sines, which gives us the following:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/2/8729a5a5ffeb27c4d48afe56ec0a14d6320d81e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sin \\theta}{5}=\\frac{1 - 2 \\sin^2 \\theta}{23} \\implies \\sin \\theta = \\frac{-23 \\pm 27}{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"335\" height=\"40\" />, \nbut since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/e/a3ebe9069e905d5b7ced1e81e69c8813e0c333e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta &lt; 180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"70\" height=\"16\" />, we go with the positive solution. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/3/ef3bd86af1e7e32b1befa106f3157e84a9640df2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin \\theta = \\frac15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"70\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>Denote the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/e/6aeaf3b3ed66bc4256b58d8123fbf178f31df9a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;C&#39;$\" width=\"37\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a65c05bd85d2609bea5db2b109ed5f556463511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. By another application of the law of sines, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/d/81d20eeaf545532de7c350719855c0350c045050.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;G = \\frac{23}{\\sqrt{24}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"93\" height=\"42\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/f/11f602665ea38ad650663a541e586aa052851079.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE = 10\\sqrt{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/6/bc67a59bebc4ce16fb276a148690ef74df28b530.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin \\theta = \\frac15, GE = \\frac{115}{\\sqrt{24}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"168\" height=\"42\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/9/599bc3519c3ca76535fde0303e337d29e2d1ab6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AG = AE - GE = 10\\sqrt{6} - \\frac{115}{\\sqrt{24}} = \\frac{5}{\\sqrt{24}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"317\" height=\"42\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/1/ea14b43d853449b9c97aa649f289050e0bbbbf57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{EB&#39;G} \\sim \\triangle{C&#39;AG}$\" width=\"151\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/3/5a3af2ee84fc3975084ea321fe2bfd99eeedc15e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{EG}{B&#39;G}=\\frac{C&#39;G}{AG} \\implies C&#39;G = \\frac{25}{\\sqrt{24}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"241\" height=\"42\" />.\n</p><p>Now we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/a/0cae058aa0302830f26ae7e969d10f5b25bfe4cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = AE + EB = 10\\sqrt{6} + 23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"238\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/f/0cf6351fc86f3a320ab04df3c8c6c1be5f170789.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;C&#39; = BC = B&#39;G + C&#39;G = \\frac{23}{\\sqrt{24}} + \\frac{25}{\\sqrt{24}} = \\frac{48}{\\sqrt{24}}=4\\sqrt{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"445\" height=\"42\" />. Thus, the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/4/1d4bb9d33362f74f749394d18e6e0506f6c25931.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(10\\sqrt{6} + 23)(4\\sqrt{6}) = 92\\sqrt{6} + 240$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"260\" height=\"21\" />, and our final answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/a/e9a476248220f81230032344b7818de1458f4ce6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$92 + 6 + 240 = \\boxed{338}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"162\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_Pre_2005\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 Pre 2005\">Mock AIME 1 Pre 2005</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_Pre_2005_Problems\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 Pre 2005 Problems\">Problems</a></b>, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/viewtopic.php?t=14769\">Source</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"